# Without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile copies EVERYTHING in the
# build context into the image layer -- including .env (real secrets: DB
# connection string, SESSION_SECRET, Adex keys, Telegram bot token) if it
# happens to exist next to the Dockerfile at build time. A baked-in secret
# in an image layer persists even if a later layer "deletes" the file, and
# leaks to anyone who can pull the image.

# Secrets -- never bake these into an image; inject at runtime instead.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Never needed inside the image (reinstalled by `npm ci` in the build step;
# an accidentally-committed local node_modules would also fight with the
# container's own platform/arch).
node_modules/

# Version control and editor metadata -- no runtime value, pure bloat/leakage.
.git/
.gitignore
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Previous build output -- must be rebuilt fresh inside the image, not
# copied in stale from the host.
dist/
.output/
.vinxi/

# Generated at dev/build time by the router plugin; regenerated by the
# image's own `npm run build` step, so copying a stale host copy in is
# unnecessary and can mask real generation failures.
src/routeTree.gen.ts

# Docs and local scratch files with no runtime purpose.
README.md
*.log
diff_*.txt
check_*.mjs
